@{
    Layout = "~/Views/Shared/_CustomerLayout.cshtml";
    ViewData["Title"] = "Privacy policy";
    ViewData["I18nTitle"] = "legal.privacyTitle";
    ViewData["LegalPage"] = "privacy";
    ViewData["LegalLede"] = "Last updated 8 September 2026. This notice is for guests using this website and Google guest accounts.";
    var fromAgreement = ViewBag.ReturnToGuestAgreement as bool? == true ? "guest-agreement" : null;
}

<section class="guest-section guest-legal-page" aria-labelledby="guestPrivacyTitle">
    <partial name="_LegalPageHead" />

    <article class="guest-legal-article">
        <section class="guest-legal-block" aria-labelledby="privacyWho">
            <h2 id="privacyWho" data-i18n="legal.privacy.whoTitle">1. Who is responsible</h2>
            <p>
                <span data-i18n="legal.privacy.whoP1Before">Mori International Hotel, AS Fortuna, Mandaue City, Cebu, is the personal information controller for guest data collected on this site. Contact us at</span>
                <a href="mailto:moriyamahotel@gmail.com">moriyamahotel@gmail.com</a>
                <span data-i18n="legal.or">or</span>
                <a href="tel:+63322388855">(032) 238 8855</a><span data-i18n="legal.period">.</span>
            </p>
            <p data-i18n="legal.privacy.whoP2">
                This policy follows the Philippines Data Privacy Act of 2012 (Republic Act No. 10173) and National Privacy Commission guidance: a privacy notice is not the same as consent. We show this notice, then ask you to tick a box before we create a guest account.
            </p>
        </section>

        <section class="guest-legal-block" aria-labelledby="privacyData">
            <h2 id="privacyData" data-i18n="legal.privacy.dataTitle">2. Personal data we collect</h2>
            <ul>
                <li data-i18n="legal.privacy.dataLi1">From Google sign-in: verified email address, name, and a Google account identifier.</li>
                <li data-i18n="legal.privacy.dataLi2">From your booking: guest names, phone number, stay dates and times, room types, guest counts, special-offer or discount requests, and messages you send us.</li>
                <li data-i18n="legal.privacy.dataLi3">From your stay: booking status, payments or receipts you upload (not full card numbers), and reviews you choose to publish.</li>
            </ul>
            <p data-i18n="legal.privacy.dataP">We do not ask for government IDs online. Senior Citizen and PWD discounts are applied by hotel staff at the front desk upon verification.</p>
        </section>

        <section class="guest-legal-block" aria-labelledby="privacyWhy">
            <h2 id="privacyWhy" data-i18n="legal.privacy.whyTitle">3. Why we use it</h2>
            <p data-i18n="legal.privacy.whyIntro">We process this data only for hotel operations:</p>
            <ul>
                <li data-i18n="legal.privacy.whyLi1">Create and sign you into a guest-level account linked to Google.</li>
                <li data-i18n="legal.privacy.whyLi2">Receive, confirm, and manage bookings and reservations.</li>
                <li data-i18n="legal.privacy.whyLi3">Contact you about your stay (including phone verification before check-in).</li>
                <li data-i18n="legal.privacy.whyLi4">Apply rates, stay fees, and offers that match your request.</li>
                <li data-i18n="legal.privacy.whyLi5">Keep records the hotel needs for accounting, security, and complaints.</li>
            </ul>
            <p data-i18n="legal.privacy.whyP">
                Account creation uses your consent (the checkbox on the guest agreement). Completing a booking also relies on the contract to provide your stay. We do not sell your personal data. We do not use this form for marketing newsletters.
            </p>
        </section>

        <section class="guest-legal-block" aria-labelledby="privacyWhoSees">
            <h2 id="privacyWhoSees" data-i18n="legal.privacy.seeTitle">4. Who can see it</h2>
            <ul>
                <li data-i18n="legal.privacy.seeLi1">Hotel staff who need it to run the front desk, rooms, and bookings.</li>
                <li data-i18n="legal.privacy.seeLi2">Google, only as the sign-in provider when you choose Continue with Google.</li>
                <li data-i18n="legal.privacy.seeLi3">When you use Mori Assistant on this site, your question and public hotel facts may be sent to Google Gemini and/or Groq to generate a reply. We do not look up your reservation in chat.</li>
                <li data-i18n="legal.privacy.seeLi4">Service providers that host this website or deliver email, under our instructions.</li>
            </ul>
            <p data-i18n="legal.privacy.seeP">Staff Google logins are separate from guest accounts and do not use this guest consent screen.</p>
        </section>

        <section class="guest-legal-block" aria-labelledby="privacyKeep">
            <h2 id="privacyKeep" data-i18n="legal.privacy.keepTitle">5. How long we keep it</h2>
            <p data-i18n="legal.privacy.keepP">
                We keep guest account and booking records for as long as the account is active and for a reasonable period afterward so we can answer stay questions, complete accounting, and meet legal duties. You may ask us to close the account or correct details using the contact information above.
            </p>
        </section>

        <section class="guest-legal-block" aria-labelledby="privacyRights">
            <h2 id="privacyRights" data-i18n="legal.privacy.rightsTitle">6. Your rights</h2>
            <p data-i18n="legal.privacy.rightsP1">Under the Data Privacy Act you may request to be informed, access your data, correct it, withdraw consent where consent is the basis we used, or object to processing that is not required to complete a stay you already requested. To use these rights, email the hotel. You may also contact the National Privacy Commission if you have a privacy complaint.</p>
            <p data-i18n="legal.privacy.rightsP2">You can stop using the guest account by logging out. Cancel on the agreement screen if you do not want an account created.</p>
        </section>

        <section class="guest-legal-block" aria-labelledby="privacySecurity">
            <h2 id="privacySecurity" data-i18n="legal.privacy.securityTitle">7. Security</h2>
            <p data-i18n="legal.privacy.securityP">
                We store account passwords with ASP.NET Identity hashing. Google guest accounts keep a fixed Google email and may also set a hotel password for email or username sign-in. Booking forms use anti-forgery tokens. We do not store raw credit-card numbers on this site.
            </p>
        </section>

        <section class="guest-legal-block" aria-labelledby="privacyRelated">
            <h2 id="privacyRelated" data-i18n="legal.privacy.relatedTitle">8. Related terms</h2>
            <p>
                <span data-i18n="legal.privacy.relatedBefore">Stay rules, rates, and cancellation are in the</span>
                <a asp-controller="Booking" asp-action="Terms" asp-route-from="@fromAgreement" data-i18n="legal.termsTitle">Terms and policies</a><span data-i18n="legal.period">.</span>
            </p>
        </section>

        <section class="guest-legal-block" aria-labelledby="privacyCookies">
            <h2 id="privacyCookies" data-i18n="legal.privacy.cookiesTitle">9. Cookies and similar storage</h2>
            <p data-i18n="legal.privacy.cookiesP1">
                We use a short cookie notice so you can choose Accept all or Necessary only. Those two choices are equal: rejecting non-essential cookies does not block booking or Google sign-in.
            </p>
            <p data-i18n="legal.privacy.cookiesIntro">Necessary cookies and similar storage (always on) keep the site working:</p>
            <ul>
                <li data-i18n="legal.privacy.cookiesLi1">Sign-in and security cookies (your session and anti-forgery tokens).</li>
                <li data-i18n="legal.privacy.cookiesLi2">Your language choice.</li>
                <li data-i18n="legal.privacy.cookiesLi3">Your cookie choice, so we do not ask on every page.</li>
            </ul>
            <p data-i18n="legal.privacy.cookiesP2">
                A stay draft (dates and rooms you started) is stored only if you choose Accept all. Necessary only does not save that short booking information. We do not currently load marketing or analytics cookies. You can change this anytime from Cookies in the footer.
            </p>
        </section>
    </article>

    <footer class="guest-legal-foot">
        <partial name="_LegalBack" />
    </footer>
</section>
